      "writtenOn": "2024-12-23T20:34:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Part of the the contract here is that this is `std::strong_equality`, so this `auto` is hiding an actual API contract that humans should be able to read (without being required to read and fully understand the whole specification of this feature to figure out what this `auto` actually might be).\n\nIn particular, we do not want any `std::*_ordering` here as we do not want to even `std::partial_ordering` of `SkRect` as that is a confusing API, and what is wanted in the Chromium side CL (for a test, which is fine there since it is tied to that specific test).",
